ODE9501 [*] Model attribute `_sql_constraints` is no longer supported since Odoo 19.0, define `models.Constraint` attributes on the model instead
  --> deprecated_sql_constraints_no_import.py:8:5
   |
 7 |     # ODE9501: `models` is not bound here, so the fix has to import it as well.
 8 |     _sql_constraints = [
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 9 |         ("name_uniq", "unique (name)", "The currency name must be unique!"),
10 |     ]
   |
help: Replace with `models.Constraint` attributes
  |
1 | from odoo.models import Model
2 + from odoo import models
3 |
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8 |     # ODE9501: `models` is not bound here, so the fix has to import it as well.
  -     _sql_constraints = [
  -         ("name_uniq", "unique (name)", "The currency name must be unique!"),
  -     ]
9 +     _name_uniq = models.Constraint("unique (name)", "The currency name must be unique!")
  |
note: This is an unsafe fix and may change runtime behavior
